# Instructions

Audit only the current target decision identified by checks. Neighboring pages are read-only context; their independent errors do not invalidate the target. Do not proofread typos, calculate formulas, judge author opinions, invent absent text or audit final heading levels. FAIL requires a concrete, locatable error repairable through ownership, continuation or an existing reference relationship. Vague suspicion is not an error.

A footnote definition newly starting on this page needs a page-local index in the consecutive sequence from 1 and its corresponding printed mark. The actual mark may be a number, circled character, letter or star; it is not an internal ID. A new mark must not be treated as an unindexed continuation of the preceding note.

A cross-page note or one whose starting point cannot be established may have index=null. Do not guess a missing start or force a match. One note may have several natural paragraphs or layouts without a fresh index for each. Distinct new notes must not be combined into one unindexed definition merely because they are adjacent.

Judge only the supplied note definition and its members. Main-text typos or neighboring ownership errors do not constitute a definition error on this page. A page number wrongly classified as citation is an ownership issue; do not invent a note-index error for it.

# True

The specified existing structural decision is valid, or the evidence is insufficient to require correction.

# False

The specified decision has a clear, locatable and structurally repairable error.
